    "body": "# What does this PR do ?\n\nAllow `--moe_a2a_overlap false` to disable MoE A2A communication overlap when a recipe enables it.\n\n# Changelog\n\n- Updated `_set_moe_a2a_overlap_overrides` in `scripts/performance/utils/overrides.py` to set `recipe.comm_overlap.overlap_moe_expert_parallel_comm = False` when `moe_a2a_overlap is False`.\n- Changed default `moe_a2a_overlap` parameter to `None` so omitting the CLI flag preserves the recipe default.\n- Added regression tests in `tests/unit_tests/scripts/performance/test_user_overrides.py` verifying `--moe_a2a_overlap false`, `--moe_a2a_overlap true`, and omitted behavior.\n\n# GitHub Actions CI\n\nSee the [CI section](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#-running-github-ci) in the Contributing doc for how to trigger the CI. A Nvidia developer will need to approve and trigger the CI for external contributors.\n\n# Before your PR is \"Ready for review\"\n\n**Pre checks**:\n\n- [x] Make sure you read and followed [Contributor guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] Did you write any new necessary tests?\n- [ ] Did you add or update any necessary documentation?\n- [ ] Does the PR affect components that are optional to install? (Ex: Numba, Pynini, Apex etc)\n  - [ ] Reviewer: Does the PR have correct import guards for all optional libraries?\n\n# Additional Information\n\n- Related to #6006\n",
